{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\n`AGENTS.md` §\"Navigating the codebase (when editing rebar itself)\" describes the Serena\nMCP server as operating over \"this checkout\". That is no longer accurate on the operator's\nhost: Serena has been re-pointed at a dedicated, filesystem-read-only clone that tracks\n`origin/main` and is refreshed by a `StartInterval=3600` LaunchAgent (the same shape as the\nexisting `com.navapbc.rebar-dev-update` agent).\n\nTwo consequences follow that an agent reading `AGENTS.md` cannot infer, and that silently\nproduce wrong conclusions:\n\n1. Serena's view is a snapshot of `origin/main`, refreshed on a poll interval, so it can\n   trail current `main` by up to that interval.\n2. It therefore never contains uncommitted work sitting in the worktree the agent is\n   actually editing.\n\nAn agent that assumes Serena indexes its own worktree will read a stale or absent symbol\nand conclude the code does not exist.\n\n## Approach\n\nAppend ONE short paragraph to the existing §\"Navigating the codebase\" section of\n`AGENTS.md`, immediately after the closing \"Cross-cutting change → do **both**…\" paragraph.\nIt states only (a) Serena reads a read-only mirror of `origin/main` rather than the local\ncheckout, and (b) that mirror auto-updates on a lag, so its answers can trail `main` and\nwill not show uncommitted worktree work.\n\nProse only, in the surrounding voice and bold-emphasis style. No table row is added; the\nexisting table is about Serena-vs-grep failure modes, which this is not.\n\n## Scope\n\nIN scope: the mirror fact and the staleness expectation, in `AGENTS.md` only.\n\nOUT of scope, deliberately, and must NOT appear in the change:\n- any warning about Serena's edit tools or write hazards\n- worktree isolation guidance\n- how the mirror or its LaunchAgent is built, located, or operated (machine-local, and\n  `CLAUDE.local.md` / `docs/*.local.md` are git-ignored — this repo change carries no\n  host-specific paths)\n- edits to `docs/code-navigation.md` or any other file\n\n## Portability\n\nDocumentation-only prose in a checked-in guidance file. It adds no code path, no command,\nno CI trigger, and no dependency on any CI provider, scheduler, or host service. The\nguidance is written host-agnostically (\"a read-only mirror of `origin/main`\", \"a poll\ninterval\") so it is equally true for any environment that points Serena at a mirror, and\nharmless where Serena is absent — that case is already covered by the section's existing\n`claude mcp get serena` pointer. Nothing in it can fail to trigger, because nothing in it\ntriggers.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The Serena section of `AGENTS.md` states that Serena reads a read-only mirror of\n      `origin/main` rather than the local checkout.\n      Proof: `grep -c 'read-only mirror' AGENTS.md` prints `1`.\n- [ ] The same paragraph states that the mirror refreshes on a lag, so Serena's answers\n      can trail current `main` and do not include uncommitted worktree work.\n      Proof: `grep -c 'uncommitted' AGENTS.md` prints `1`, and `grep -c 'trail' AGENTS.md`\n      prints `1`.\n- [ ] No file other than `AGENTS.md` is modified.\n      Proof: `git diff --name-only origin/main` prints exactly the single line `AGENTS.md`.\n- [ ] The addition is confined to the named section: it lands after the \"Cross-cutting\n      change\" paragraph and before the `## Git workflow` heading, and the diff is\n      additions only.\n      Proof: `git diff --numstat origin/main -- AGENTS.md` reports `0` deletions, and\n      `awk '/^## Navigating the codebase/,/^## Git workflow/' AGENTS.md | grep -c 'read-only mirror'`\n      prints `1`.\n- [ ] Out-of-scope topics are absent: the addition names neither Serena's edit tools, nor\n      write/edit hazards, nor worktree isolation, nor any host-specific path or LaunchAgent.\n      Proof: `git diff origin/main -- AGENTS.md | grep -icE 'replace_symbol|insert_after|edit tool|launchagent|/Users/'`\n      prints `0`.\n\n## Testing\n\nThis change is documentation prose, so it carries no unit test; it is proven by the\nacceptance-criteria commands above plus the repository's standing gates, all run from the\nchange's own worktree before push:\n\n- `make lint` — ruff check + format-check (the commit gate), expected to exit 0.\n- `make typecheck` — mypy, expected to exit 0.\n- `pytest tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py` — the module-size contract. This is a\n  CI-only gate that `make lint` does NOT run, so it is run explicitly; expected to pass.\n- `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` — the shrink-only complexity\n  ratchet, expected to report `new=0` and `increased=0`.\n\nA prose-only change cannot regress any of the four, so a failure in any of them is\nevidence the diff touched more than `AGENTS.md` and must be investigated before push, not\nretried.\n\nFinal verification is the Gerrit gate itself: the change is not landed until it carries\n`LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1` (CI green on GitHub Actions) with no unresolved comments.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] `AGENTS.md` edited as above; every acceptance criterion verified by running its\n      stated proof command.\n- [ ] All four commands in `## Testing` run and pass.\n- [ ] Change pushed to `refs/for/main`, carries `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`, no\n      unresolved comments, and is submitted/merged.\n\n## File impact\n\n- `AGENTS.md` — append one paragraph to the \"Navigating the codebase\" section.\n"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787950960448230977,"uuid":"43c0e180-646e-4575-a1ea-5503b9dc9b73"}